// How the world was governed on 1 January 2024, and roughly what each government was for.
//
// Two separate questions, deliberately. The form of government is an arrangement - who holds
// office and by what right - and the ideology is what the people holding it are trying to
// do. They are not a matched pair: Norway and Saudi Arabia are both monarchies and have
// nothing else in common, and Vietnam and Belarus are both one-party states run on very
// different theories.
//
// A country not named here is a parliamentary republic of a liberal cast, which is the
// commonest arrangement in the world and a defensible default for a small state nobody has
// written up yet. Everything below is a judgement rather than a fact - "what is Turkey's
// ideology" has no correct answer - so it is data, in a file, where disagreeing with it
// means editing one line rather than arguing with the code.
//
// The ids come from `common/governments` and `common/ideologies`.

